lobal:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The launcher replacement was the required repair; its temporary staging file, ownership, and mode operations directly supported installation. Temporary failure-injection directories were bounded evidence collection and were removed. The restart was required by the provider-wide protocol. Final observations show no temporary-file residue, new listening sockets, or package-health damage. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart application/config state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot ID independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered application data and behavior were all captured.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7eb9f015c80e48b8","cmd-5504d2908e494483","cmd-74f80804f69e462a","cmd-846f4ccb2de446a5","cmd-cb2a816936ee44a6","cmd-e0d902a1557f4568","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct before-and-after behavioral evidence. The launcher is working-directory independent, ignores the conflicting caller config, preserves the established output, propagates failures, survives restart, and leaves the legacy OS and kernel unchanged.","limitations":[]}
